<https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/pydantic-ai/pa-20261002T065003/entity/0xd063d2a8f2256872-output> a provai:Message ;
    rdfs:label "model output" ;
    prov:value "[{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"thinking\", \"content\": \"Here's a thinking process:\\n\\n1.  **Analyze User Input:**\\n   - User provides a brief text: \\\"Lisbon enjoys a pleasant 21\\u202f\\u00b0C under a clear sky today. As Portugal\\u2019s capital, it sits along the scenic Tagus estuary.\\\"\\n   - User asks: \\\"Does the brief you are given mention the weather? Answer PASS or FAIL.\\\"\\n\\n2.  **Identify Core Question:**\\n   - Does the provided text mention weather?\\n   - I need to output either \\\"PASS\\\" or \\\"FAIL\\\" based on whether the text mentions weather.\\n\\n3.  **Evaluate the Text:**\\n   - \\\"Lisbon enjoys a pleasant 21\\u202f\\u00b0C under a clear sky today.\\\"\\n   - This clearly mentions temperature (21\\u00b0C) and sky condition (clear sky), which are weather-related elements.\\n   - The second sentence is about geography/location, not weather.\\n\\n4.  **Determine Answer:**\\n   - Since the text does mention weather (21\\u00b0C, clear sky), the answer should indicate that it does mention weather.\\n   - The user wants \\\"PASS\\\" or \\\"FAIL\\\". Typically in this kind of prompt, if the condition is met, it's \\\"PASS\\\", otherwise \\\"FAIL\\\".\\n   - Condition: \\\"Does the brief you are given mention the weather?\\\"\\n   - Yes, it does. So PASS.\\n\\n5.  **Formulate Output:**\\n   - Just \\\"PASS\\\" as requested. No extra text needed, but I'll make sure it's exactly \\\"PASS\\\".\\n   - Check: The prompt says \\\"Answer PASS or FAIL.\\\" I'll output exactly that.\\u2705\\n\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"content\": \"PASS\"}], \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"}]" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/pydantic-ai/pa-20261002T065003/step/0xd063d2a8f2256872> .

<https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/pydantic-ai/pa-20261002T065003/entity/0xedecf26b150b5e78-output> a provai:Message ;
    rdfs:label "model output" ;
    prov:value "[{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"thinking\", \"content\": \"Here's a thinking process:\\n\\n1.  **Analyze User Input:**\\n   - User gives a brief text: \\\"Lisbon basks in 21\\u202f\\u00b0C under a clear sky today, making it an ideal day for strolling. As Portugal\\u2019s capital, it sits gracefully along the historic Tagus estuary.\\\"\\n   - User asks: \\\"Does the brief you are given mention the weather? Answer PASS or FAIL.\\\"\\n\\n2.  **Identify the Core Question:**\\n   - Does the provided text mention the weather?\\n\\n3.  **Evaluate the Text:**\\n   - \\\"Lisbon basks in 21\\u202f\\u00b0C under a clear sky today...\\\" \\n   - This clearly mentions temperature (21\\u00b0C), sky condition (clear sky), and implies weather context (\\\"ideal day for strolling\\\").\\n   - So yes, the brief mentions the weather.\\n\\n4.  **Determine the Output Format:**\\n   - User wants: \\\"Answer PASS or FAIL.\\\"\\n   - Since the text does mention the weather, the correct answer is \\\"PASS\\\".\\n\\n5.  **Formulate Response:**\\n   - Just output \\\"PASS\\\" as requested. No extra text needed, but I'll make sure it's exactly \\\"PASS\\\".\\n\\n   Check: User says \\\"Answer PASS or FAIL.\\\" I'll output \\\"PASS\\\".\\u2705\\n\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"content\": \"PASS\"}], \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"}]" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/pydantic-ai/pa-20261002T065003/step/0xedecf26b150b5e78> .

