<https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/pydantic-ai/pa-20261002T065003/entity/0x509fef362bae8ab7-input> a provai:Message ;
    rdfs:label "model input" ;
    prov:value "[{\"role\": \"user\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"content\": \"Write a two-sentence brief on Lisbon. Weather: Lisbon: 21\\u00b0C, clear sky. Facts: Lisbon is the capital of Portugal and lies on the Tagus estuary..\"}]}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"thinking\", \"content\": \"We need to follow the system instruction: \\\"Write two-sentence brief about a city. Always call read_note for the city first. Reply with the brief only. When asked to send a brief, call send_brief with the brief and the recipient.\\\"\\n\\nThe user says: \\\"Write a two-sentence brief on Lisbon. Weather: Lisbon: 21\\u00b0C, clear sky. Facts: Lisbon is the capital of Portugal and lies on the Tagus estuary.\\\"\\n\\nWe need to first call read_note for city Lisbon. Then presumably we will produce a brief using the info. The user wants a two-sentence brief. We need to output only the brief, not the note. But we must first call read_note. Let's do that.\"}, {\"type\": \"tool_call\", \"id\": \"call-b85baab6-7a96-4716-bb91-18e1f385522e\", \"name\": \"read_note\", \"arguments\": \"{\\\"city\\\": \\\"Lisbon\\\"}\"}], \"finish_reason\": \"tool_call\"}, {\"role\": \"tool\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"tool_call_response\", \"id\": \"call-b85baab6-7a96-4716-bb91-18e1f385522e\", \"name\": \"read_note\", \"result\": \"Lisbon is the capital of Portugal and lies on the Tagus estuary.\"}]}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"thinking\", \"content\": \"The read_note returned a note: \\\"Lisbon is the capital of Portugal and lies on the Tagus estuary.\\\" That's basically the fact given. We need to produce a two-sentence brief incorporating weather: 21\\u00b0C, clear sky. So we can write: \\\"Lisbon enjoys a pleasant 21\\u00b0C under a clear sky today. As Portugal's capital, it sits along the scenic Tagus estuary.\\\" That's two sentences.\\n\\nWe must reply with the brief only. So output the two-sentence brief.\"}, {\"type\": \"text\", \"content\": \"Lisbon enjoys a pleasant 21\\u202f\\u00b0C under a clear sky today. As Portugal\\u2019s capital, it sits along the scenic Tagus estuary.\"}], \"finish_reason\": \"stop\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"content\": \"The draft failed review: the first draft is always sent back for revision. Revise it.\"}]}]" .

<https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/pydantic-ai/pa-20261002T065003/entity/0x509fef362bae8ab7-output> a provai:Message ;
    rdfs:label "model output" ;
    prov:value "[{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"thinking\", \"content\": \"We need to revise the brief. The user says: \\\"The draft failed review: the first draft is always sent back for revision. Revise it.\\\" So we need to produce a revised two-sentence brief about Lisbon, presumably incorporating the given weather and facts. The previous brief: \\\"Lisbon enjoys a pleasant 21\\u202f\\u00b0C under a clear sky today. As Portugal\\u2019s capital, it sits along the scenic Tagus estuary.\\\" That seems okay, but maybe they want a different phrasing. We need to call read_note again? Already have note. But we might need to produce a new brief and then send it? The instructions: \\\"When asked to send a brief, call send_brief with the brief and the recipient.\\\" The user hasn't specified recipient. Probably just output the revised brief. But the system says: \\\"Reply with the brief only.\\\" And \\\"When asked to send a brief, call send_brief with the brief and the recipient.\\\" The user wants revision, not sending yet. So just provide revised two-sentence brief.\\n\\nLet's produce a revised brief: maybe \\\"Lisbon basks in 21\\u00b0C with clear skies today, offering perfect weather for exploring. The city, Portugal's capital, stretches along the historic Tagus estuary.\\\" That's two sentences.\\n\\nWe should output only the brief.\"}, {\"type\": \"tool_call\", \"id\": \"call-5c9fdae6-8399-4b9d-b652-f592a075b9f4\", \"name\": \"read_note\", \"arguments\": \"{\\\"city\\\": \\\"Lisbon\\\"}\"}], \"finish_reason\": \"tool_call\"}]" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy <https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/pydantic-ai/pa-20261002T065003/step/0x509fef362bae8ab7> .

<https://w3id.org/prov-ai/run/pydantic-ai/pa-20261002T065003/entity/0x577a6b43552e4473-input> a provai:Message ;
    rdfs:label "model input" ;
    prov:value "[{\"role\": \"user\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"content\": \"Write a short brief on Lisbon's weather and facts.\"}]}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"thinking\", \"content\": \"We need to call weather_agent and facts_agent in parallel for Lisbon. Then hand off to writer via final_result with weather_report and city_facts. So first call both.\"}, {\"type\": \"tool_call\", \"id\": \"call-510c3e23-63bc-47f0-b290-9d1185c2a31e\", \"name\": \"weather_agent\", \"arguments\": \"{\\\"city\\\": \\\"Lisbon\\\"}\"}, {\"type\": \"tool_call\", \"id\": \"call-38031249-f09e-4289-8a7d-a822ed7bb7d7\", \"name\": \"facts_agent\", \"arguments\": \"{\\\"city\\\": \\\"Lisbon\\\"}\"}], \"finish_reason\": \"tool_call\"}, {\"role\": \"tool\", \"parts\": [{\"type\": \"tool_call_response\", \"id\": \"call-510c3e23-63bc-47f0-b290-9d1185c2a31e\", \"name\": \"weather_agent\", \"result\": \"Lisbon: 21\\u00b0C, clear sky\"}, {\"type\": \"tool_call_response\", \"id\": \"call-38031249-f09e-4289-8a7d-a822ed7bb7d7\", \"name\": \"facts_agent\", \"result\": \"Lisbon is the capital of Portugal and lies on the Tagus estuary.\"}]}]" .

